module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.NaiveCotangent.Quotient
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Noetherian.ArtinRees
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.NaiveCotangent.Homology

/-!
# The conormal comparison of Stacks 0AJS (1)

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring, let `I ⊆ A` be an ideal, let `B` be an object of the category
(Stacks 0AL4), and fix a completed polynomial presentation `B = A⟨x₁, …, x_r⟩ / J`, where
`A⟨x⟩ = A[x₁, …, x_r]^∧` is the `I`-adic completion of a polynomial algebra.  Writing
`Aₙ = A / Iⁿ` and `Bₙ = B / IⁿB`, the presentation induces presentations
`Bₙ = Aₙ[x₁, …, x_r] / Jₙ` with

`Jₙ = J / (J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩)`,

and Stacks 0AJS (1) asserts that the two inverse systems of two-term complexes
`{NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ}` and `{NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}}` are *strictly* pro-isomorphic: there is a single
`c ≥ 0` such that for every `n ≥ c` there are canonical surjections

`NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ ⟶ NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ} ⟶ NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B B_{n-c}`

compatible with the transition maps of both systems.

This file proves that comparison.  Two reductions make it short.  First, **the degree-`0`
terms are not shifted at all**: `(⨁ᵢ B dxᵢ) ⊗_B Bₙ = ⨁ᵢ Bₙ dxᵢ` on the nose, so both
systems have literally the same degree-`0` term `(Fin r → B) / Iⁿ(Fin r → B)` and the
comparison is the identity there.  Second, the entire shift-by-`c` content is therefore the
single sandwich of ideals of `A⟨x⟩`

`Iⁿ J ⊆ J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩ ⊆ I^{n-c} J`,  `n ≥ c`,

whose right-hand inclusion is the Artin–Rees lemma (Stacks 00IN, already available in this
library as `artin_rees`) applied to the submodule `J` of the Noetherian ring `A⟨x⟩` (Stacks
0AJQ).  Passing to `J / J²` turns the sandwich into a sandwich of submodules of the conormal
module, and the generic machinery of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/NaiveCotangent/Quotient.lean` turns *that* into the two chain maps.

## Main definitions

* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.conormalSub`: the submodule of `J / J²` generated by
  the image of `J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`, so that `(J / J²) / conormalSub n = Jₙ / Jₙ²`.
* `Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex.reducedComplex`: the two-term complex
  `Jₙ / Jₙ² ⟶ ⨁ᵢ Bₙ dxᵢ`, which is `NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}`.

## Main results

* `Rig.exists_artinRees_sandwich`: the ideal sandwich `𝔞ⁿ J ⊆ J ⊓ 𝔞ⁿ ⊆ 𝔞^{n-c} J` in a
  Noetherian ring, read off `artin_rees`.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.smul_top_le_conormalSub`: the left-hand inclusion
  `Iⁿ · (J / J²) ⊆ conormalSub n`, valid for every `n`.
* `Rig.CompletedPolynomialPresentation.exists_conormalSub_le_smul_top`: the right-hand
  inclusion `conormalSub n ⊆ I^{n-c} · (J / J²)` for a uniform `c`.
* `Rig.CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex.exists_proIsomorphism_comparison`: **Stacks 0AJS (1)**
  for the chosen presentation — the two degreewise surjective comparison chain maps, with
  composite the transition map of `{NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ}`.

## Implementation notes

`reducedComplex` is `NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}` *presented as a quotient of `NL^∧_{B/A}`*, which is how the
source produces it and is exactly what the comparison needs.  Identifying its degree-`-1`
term `J / (J² + (J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩))` with the conormal module of a genuine
`Algebra.Generators Aₙ Bₙ (Fin r)` — that is, realising `Aₙ[x] = A⟨x⟩ / Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` and `Jₙ` as
an ideal of it — is the other half of Stacks 0AJS (1) and is not done here; neither tag is
claimed.

The conormal submodule is the `B`-span of the image of `J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`, because
`Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk` is linear over `A⟨x⟩` rather than over `B`.  The three
inclusions it has to satisfy are proved by the colon-ideal reformulation
(`Submodule.mem_colon` together with `Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap`), which replaces an
induction over `Ideal.map` membership by a statement about elements of `I` itself; that is
what `map_smul_top_le_map_smul_top` and `smul_top_le_conormalSub` both run on.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AJS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AJS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00IN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00IN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AJQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AJQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AL4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AL4)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Algebra Function

namespace NaiveCotangent.TwoTerm

universe u v w

variable {S : Type u} [CommRing S] (X : TwoTerm.{u, v, w} S)

/-- The canonical surjection of `X` onto the quotient complex `X₁ / U ⟶ X₀ / V`, given a
compatible pair of submodules.  Both components are the quotient maps. -/
public def quotProj (U : Submodule S X.X₁) (V : Submodule S X.X₀) (h : U ≤ V.comap X.d) :
    ChainMap X (X.quotBy U V h) where
  f₁ := U.mkQ
  f₀ := V.mkQ
  comm := LinearMap.ext fun _ => rfl

end NaiveCotangent.TwoTerm

namespace Rig

/-! ## Generic ingredients -/

/-- **The Artin–Rees sandwich.**  Let `R` be a Noetherian ring and let `𝔞`, `J` be ideals of
`R`.  Then there is a `c > 0` such that for every `n ≥ c`

`𝔞ⁿ J ⊆ J ⊓ 𝔞ⁿ ⊆ 𝔞^{n-c} J`.

The left inclusion is formal; the right one is the Artin–Rees lemma (Stacks 00IN) for the
submodule `J` of `R`.  This is the only place where the shift by `c` in Stacks 0AJS (1)
comes from. -/
public theorem exists_artinRees_sandwich {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (𝔞 J : Ideal R) :
    ∃ c > 0, ∀ n ≥ c, 𝔞 ^ n * J ≤ J ⊓ 𝔞 ^ n ∧ J ⊓ 𝔞 ^ n ≤ 𝔞 ^ (n - c) * J := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc0, hc⟩ := artin_rees (M := R) 𝔞 J
  have htop : ∀ m : ℕ, 𝔞 ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule R R) = 𝔞 ^ m := fun m => by
    rw [Ideal.smul_eq_mul, Ideal.mul_top]
  refine ⟨c, hc0, fun n hn => ⟨le_inf Ideal.mul_le_right Ideal.mul_le_left, ?_⟩⟩
  have h := hc n hn
  rw [htop, htop] at h
  rw [inf_comm, h, ← Ideal.smul_eq_mul]
  exact Submodule.smul_mono le_rfl inf_le_right

/-- If `𝔞` moves every element of `M` into `N`, then `𝔞 R · M ⊆ N`; checking on generators
`algebraMap A R a` of the extended ideal suffices. -/
private theorem map_smul_top_le_of_forall_smul_mem {A R M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing R]
    [Algebra A R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (𝔞 : Ideal A) (N : Submodule R M)
    (h : ∀ a ∈ 𝔞, ∀ y : M, algebraMap A R a • y ∈ N) :
    (𝔞.map (algebraMap A R)) • (⊤ : Submodule R M) ≤ N := by
  have hcol : 𝔞.map (algebraMap A R) ≤ N.colon Set.univ :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha =>
      Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (Submodule.mem_colon.mpr fun y _ => h a ha y)
  exact Submodule.smul_le.mpr fun r hr y _ =>
    Submodule.mem_colon.mp (hcol hr) y (Set.mem_univ y)

/-- For a tower of rings `A → R → S` and an `S`-module `M`, the submodule of `M` generated
by `𝔞 M` for an ideal `𝔞 ⊆ A` does not grow when the scalars are enlarged from `R` to `S`:
every element of `𝔞 R · M` is already an element of `𝔞 S · M`.

Only this direction is needed: it is what converts a statement about the `A⟨x⟩`-action on
`J / J²` into a statement about the `B`-action. -/
public theorem map_smul_top_le_map_smul_top {A R S M : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra A R] [Algebra A S] [Algebra R S] [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M]
    [Module R M] [Module S M] [IsScalarTower A R M] [IsScalarTower A S M] [IsScalarTower R S M]
    (𝔞 : Ideal A) :
    (𝔞.map (algebraMap A R)) • (⊤ : Submodule R M) ≤
      Submodule.restrictScalars R ((𝔞.map (algebraMap A S)) • (⊤ : Submodule S M)) := by
  refine map_smul_top_le_of_forall_smul_mem 𝔞 _ fun a ha y => ?_
  have hy : (algebraMap A R a) • y = (algebraMap A S a) • y := by
    simp only [algebraMap_smul]
  rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem, hy]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha) Submodule.mem_top

/-- A tuple of a finite free module all of whose entries lie in an ideal `𝔞` lies in
`𝔞 · (⨁ S)`.  This is the degree-`0` half of the comparison of Stacks 0AJS (1): the free
module `⨁ᵢ B dxᵢ` is reduced modulo `IⁿB` entry by entry. -/
public theorem mem_smul_top_of_forall_mem {S : Type*} [CommRing S] {r : ℕ} {𝔞 : Ideal S}
    {v : Fin r → S} (hv : ∀ i, v i ∈ 𝔞) : v ∈ 𝔞 • (⊤ : Submodule S (Fin r → S)) := by
  classical
  rw [← Finset.univ_sum_single v]
  refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
  have hsingle : Pi.single i (v i) = v i • Pi.single i (1 : S) := by
    ext j
    rcases eq_or_ne j i with h | h
    · subst h; simp
    · simp [Pi.single_eq_of_ne h]
  rw [hsingle]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem_smul (hv i) Submodule.mem_top

/-- A derivation over `A` preserves every ideal of `R` generated by the image of an ideal of
`A`: on a generator `algebraMap A R a` the derivation vanishes, and the Leibniz rule keeps
the Lie bracket inside the ideal.  For the completed polynomial algebra this says that the
formal partial derivatives carry `Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` into `Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`, which is the degree-`0`
compatibility of the comparison of Stacks 0AJS (1). -/
public theorem derivation_mem_map_of_mem_map {A R : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing R]
    [Algebra A R] (D : Derivation A R R) (𝔞 : Ideal A) {x : R}
    (hx : x ∈ 𝔞.map (algebraMap A R)) : D x ∈ 𝔞.map (algebraMap A R) := by
  set 𝔎 : Ideal R := 𝔞.map (algebraMap A R) with h𝔎
  have hT : ∃ T : Ideal R, ∀ y : R, y ∈ T ↔ y ∈ 𝔎 ∧ D y ∈ 𝔎 := by
    refine ⟨{ carrier := {y : R | y ∈ 𝔎 ∧ D y ∈ 𝔎}
              add_mem' := fun {y z} hy hz =>
                ⟨𝔎.add_mem hy.1 hz.1, by rw [map_add]; exact 𝔎.add_mem hy.2 hz.2⟩
              zero_mem' := ⟨𝔎.zero_mem, by rw [map_zero]; exact 𝔎.zero_mem⟩
              smul_mem' := fun s {y} hy => ⟨𝔎.smul_mem s hy.1, ?_⟩ }, fun _ => Iff.rfl⟩
    rw [smul_eq_mul, D.leibniz, smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    exact 𝔎.add_mem (𝔎.mul_mem_left s hy.2) (𝔎.mul_mem_right _ hy.1)
  obtain ⟨T, hTmem⟩ := hT
  have hsub : 𝔎 ≤ T := by
    refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => Ideal.mem_comap.mpr ?_
    exact (hTmem _).mpr ⟨Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha, by
      rw [D.map_algebraMap]; exact 𝔎.zero_mem⟩
  exact ((hTmem x).mp (hsub hx)).2

/-- The preimage of `𝔞 J` in `J` is `𝔞 · J`, where `J` is regarded as an `R`-module through
its own inclusion.  This is the step that lets the Artin–Rees sandwich, an inclusion of
ideals of `R`, be read as an inclusion of submodules of `J`. -/
public theorem comap_subtype_mul_eq_smul_top {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (J 𝔞 : Ideal R) :
    Submodule.comap (J.subtype) (𝔞 * J) = 𝔞 • (⊤ : Submodule R J) := by
  have hmap : Submodule.map (J.subtype) (𝔞 • (⊤ : Submodule R J)) = 𝔞 * J := by
    rw [Submodule.map_smul'', Submodule.map_top, Submodule.range_subtype, Ideal.smul_eq_mul]
  rw [← hmap]
  exact Submodule.comap_map_eq_self (by rw [Submodule.ker_subtype]; exact bot_le)

/-! ## The conormal submodule cut out by `J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` -/

namespace CompletedPolynomialPresentation

universe u v

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A} {B : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
  (P : CompletedPolynomialPresentation I B)

/-- The ideal `Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` of the completed polynomial algebra of a presentation. -/
public noncomputable abbrev adicPow (n : ℕ) : Ideal P.extension.Ring :=
  (I ^ n).map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)

/-- The submodule of the conormal module `J / J²` generated by the image of
`J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`.  The quotient `(J / J²) / conormalSub n` is `Jₙ / Jₙ²`, the degree-`-1` term
of `NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}`, since `Jₙ = J / (J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩)` and the modular law gives
`Jₙ / Jₙ² = J / (J² + (J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩))`. -/
public noncomputable def conormalSub (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule B.carrier P.extension.Cotangent :=
  Submodule.span B.carrier
    (⇑(Extension.Cotangent.mk (P := P.extension)) ''
      {g : P.extension.ker | (g : P.extension.Ring) ∈ P.adicPow n})

/-- A class `mk g` with `g ∈ J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` lies in `conormalSub n`. -/
public theorem mk_mem_conormalSub {n : ℕ} (g : P.extension.ker)
    (hg : (g : P.extension.Ring) ∈ P.adicPow n) :
    Extension.Cotangent.mk g ∈ P.conormalSub n :=
  Submodule.subset_span ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩

/-- **The left-hand inclusion of the Artin–Rees sandwich, in the conormal module.**
`Iⁿ · (J / J²) ⊆ conormalSub n`, valid for every `n` with no shift: it only uses
`Iⁿ J ⊆ J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`, which is formal.  Together with
`exists_conormalSub_le_smul_top` this is the sandwich of Stacks 0AJS (1). -/
public theorem smul_top_le_conormalSub (n : ℕ) :
    (B.adicIdeal ^ n) • (⊤ : Submodule B.carrier P.extension.Cotangent) ≤ P.conormalSub n := by
  have hpow : B.adicIdeal ^ n = (I ^ n).map (algebraMap A B.carrier) :=
    (Ideal.map_pow (algebraMap A B.carrier) I n).symm
  rw [hpow]
  refine map_smul_top_le_of_forall_smul_mem (I ^ n) _ fun a ha y => ?_
  obtain ⟨g, rfl⟩ := Extension.Cotangent.mk_surjective (P := P.extension) y
  have hsmul : (algebraMap A B.carrier a) • Extension.Cotangent.mk g
      = Extension.Cotangent.mk ((algebraMap A P.extension.Ring a) • g) := by
    rw [map_smul]
    simp only [algebraMap_smul]
  rw [hsmul]
  refine P.mk_mem_conormalSub _ ?_
  exact (P.adicPow n).mul_mem_right _ (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha)

/-- **The right-hand inclusion of the Artin–Rees sandwich, in the conormal module.**  There
is a `c > 0` such that for every `n ≥ c` one has `conormalSub n ⊆ I^{n-c} · (J / J²)`.  This
is Artin–Rees (Stacks 00IN) in the Noetherian ring `A⟨x⟩` (Stacks 0AJQ), transported to
`J / J²` along `Algebra.Extension.Cotangent.mk`. -/
public theorem exists_conormalSub_le_smul_top [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    ∃ c > 0, ∀ n ≥ c, P.conormalSub n ≤
      (B.adicIdeal ^ (n - c)) • (⊤ : Submodule B.carrier P.extension.Cotangent) := by
  let _ : IsNoetherianRing P.extension.Ring := AdicCompletion.isNoetherianRing _
  obtain ⟨c, hc0, hc⟩ :=
    exists_artinRees_sandwich (I.map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)) P.extension.ker
  refine ⟨c, hc0, fun n hn => Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
  have hmem : (g : P.extension.Ring) ∈
      P.extension.ker ⊓ (I.map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)) ^ n :=
    ⟨g.2, by rwa [← Ideal.map_pow]⟩
  have hJ : g ∈ (I.map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)) ^ (n - c) •
      (⊤ : Submodule P.extension.Ring P.extension.ker) := by
    rw [← comap_subtype_mul_eq_smul_top]
    exact (hc n hn).2 hmem
  have hcot : Extension.Cotangent.mk g ∈
      (I.map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)) ^ (n - c) •
        (⊤ : Submodule P.extension.Ring P.extension.Cotangent) := by
    have := Submodule.mem_map_of_mem (f := Extension.Cotangent.mk (P := P.extension)) hJ
    rw [Submodule.map_smul''] at this
    exact Submodule.smul_mono le_rfl le_top this
  have hbridge := map_smul_top_le_map_smul_top (A := A) (R := P.extension.Ring)
    (S := B.carrier) (M := P.extension.Cotangent) (I ^ (n - c))
  rw [Ideal.map_pow] at hbridge
  have := hbridge hcot
  rw [Submodule.restrictScalars_mem] at this
  rwa [← Ideal.map_pow (algebraMap A B.carrier) I (n - c)]

end CompletedPolynomialPresentation

/-! ## The comparison of two-term complexes -/

namespace CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex

universe u v

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A} {B : AdicFiniteTypeAlgebra.{u, v} A I}
  {P : CompletedPolynomialPresentation I B}

/-- The differential of `NL^∧_{B/A}` carries the image of `J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩` into
`Iⁿ · (⨁ᵢ B dxᵢ)`: on a class `mk g` the differential is the tuple of formal partial
derivatives of `g`, and a derivation over `A` preserves the ideal `Iⁿ A⟨x⟩`. -/
public theorem conormalSub_le_comap_differential (K : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P)
    (n : ℕ) :
    P.conormalSub n ≤ Submodule.comap K.differential
      ((B.adicIdeal ^ n) • (⊤ : Submodule B.carrier (Fin P.variableCount → B.carrier))) := by
  refine Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_
  rintro _ ⟨g, hg, rfl⟩
  rw [SetLike.mem_coe, Submodule.mem_comap, K.differential_mk g]
  refine mem_smul_top_of_forall_mem fun i => ?_
  -- The formal partial derivative and the presentation map are declared on
  -- `P.completedPolynomialRing`; name copies of them typed on `P.extension.Ring`, the ring
  -- carrying `J` and its conormal module, so that the two spellings never meet in a rewrite.
  let D : Derivation A P.extension.Ring P.extension.Ring := K.partialDeriv i
  let f : P.extension.Ring →ₐ[A] B.carrier := P.toAlgHom
  have hder : D (g : P.extension.Ring) ∈ (I ^ n).map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring) :=
    derivation_mem_map_of_mem_map D (I ^ n) hg
  have hcomp : (f.toRingHom).comp (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)
      = algebraMap A B.carrier :=
    f.comp_algebraMap
  have himg : f (D (g : P.extension.Ring)) ∈
      ((I ^ n).map (algebraMap A P.extension.Ring)).map (f.toRingHom) :=
    Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hder
  rwa [Ideal.map_map, hcomp, Ideal.map_pow] at himg

/-- **`NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}`**, as a two-term complex of `B`-modules: `Jₙ / Jₙ² ⟶ ⨁ᵢ Bₙ dxᵢ`,
produced as the quotient of `NL^∧_{B/A}` by the pair of submodules
`(J ∩ Iⁿ A⟨x⟩) · (J / J²)` in degree `-1` and `Iⁿ · (⨁ᵢ B dxᵢ)` in degree `0`.  The
degree-`0` term is the same as that of `NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ`, with no shift. -/
public noncomputable def reducedComplex (K : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P) (n : ℕ) :
    NaiveCotangent.TwoTerm B.carrier :=
  K.twoTerm.quotBy (P.conormalSub n) ((B.adicIdeal ^ n) • ⊤)
    (K.conormalSub_le_comap_differential n)

/-- **Stacks 0AJS (1)** for a fixed completed polynomial presentation `B = A⟨x⟩ / J`: the two
inverse systems `{NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ}` and `{NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ}}` of two-term complexes of
`B`-modules are strictly pro-isomorphic.  Concretely, there is a `c > 0` such that for every
`n ≥ c` there are chain maps

`NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ --φ--> NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ} --ψ--> NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B B_{n-c}`,

surjective in both degrees, whose composite is the transition map
`NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B Bₙ → NL^∧_{B/A} ⊗_B B_{n-c}` of the first system.  Composing `ψ` with the
`φ` at level `n - c` gives the chain
`NL^∧ ⊗ Bₙ → NL_{Bₙ/Aₙ} → NL^∧ ⊗ B_{n-c} → NL_{B_{n-c}/A_{n-c}}` of the source. -/
public theorem exists_proIsomorphism_comparison [IsNoetherianRing A]
    (K : CompletedNaiveCotangentComplex P) :
    ∃ c > 0, ∀ n ≥ c,
      ∃ (φ : NaiveCotangent.ChainMap (K.twoTerm.modIdeal (B.adicIdeal ^ n))
                (K.reducedComplex n))
        (ψ : NaiveCotangent.ChainMap (K.reducedComplex n)
                (K.twoTerm.modIdeal (B.adicIdeal ^ (n - c)))),
        Surjective φ.f₁ ∧ Surjective φ.f₀ ∧ Surjective ψ.f₁ ∧ Surjective ψ.f₀ ∧
          ψ.comp φ = K.twoTerm.modIdealMap (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Nat.sub_le n c)) := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc0, hc⟩ := P.exists_conormalSub_le_smul_top
  refine ⟨c, hc0, fun n hn => ⟨
    K.twoTerm.quotByMap (K.twoTerm.smul_top_le_comap_d (B.adicIdeal ^ n))
      (K.conormalSub_le_comap_differential n) (P.smul_top_le_conormalSub n) le_rfl,
    K.twoTerm.quotByMap (K.conormalSub_le_comap_differential n)
      (K.twoTerm.smul_top_le_comap_d (B.adicIdeal ^ (n - c))) (hc n hn)
